{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The draft is largely faithful to the inventor's disclosure, with all claims and descriptive text being well-supported. The application is internally consistent and free of drafting placeholders.\n\nHowever, I found one critical disclosure-fidelity issue. The briefs for two figures introduce specific, unsupported geometric details for a key functional part, the rigid spacer frame. The inventor's source defines this part by its function and the passages it creates, not by a specific cross-sectional shape. The figure briefs describe the frame as being constructed from \"webs,\" which is a specific structural choice that adds technical substance not present in the source. This must be corrected to ensure the drawings are a schematic representation of the disclosed invention, rather than an over-specification that narrows the invention or introduces an unsupported embodiment.\n\nThe finding below details the issue and provides a complete, filing-clean fix. After this correction, the application should be fully compliant with the source materials."}
